INT. ER NURSES' STATION - 3 A.M.

Fluorescent lights. A whiteboard of patient names. A coffee pot at its last inch.

DR. NKECHI ADEBAYO, 30s, charts. Orderly LUIS FERNANDEZ, 20s, mops. Dr. HENRY WU, 40s, drinks from a mug that reads WORLD'S OKAYEST DOC.

The overhead speaker clicks. It is Nurse Grace Tolliver at triage.

GRACE (V.O.)
Code blue, bay six. Code blue, bay six.

Nkechi drops her pen.

NKECHI
(to the room)
Bay six. Go.

NURSE GRACE TOLLIVER, 50s, bursts around the corner pushing the crash cart.

GRACE
Got the cart.

HENRY
Who's in six?

LUIS
The kid. Car accident.

NKECHI
(already moving)
Luis, ambu bag.

LUIS
On it.

They sprint. Henry, lingering, mutters to himself.

HENRY
(under his breath)
Please be the dog. Please be the dog.

He sets down the mug and follows. The whiteboard marker rolls off the ledge and clatters on the floor.

At the end of the hall a curtain whips open. A small, familiar bark.

NKECHI (O.S.)
It's a dog!

GRACE (O.S.)
It's a golden retriever!

LUIS (O.S.)
Doc, he's waking up!

HENRY
(sagging)
Thank God.
